    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0093" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.014/5–2147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Italy </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-28T18:00:00-04:00">May 28, 1947—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>787. If Yugos decline participate provisional demarcation FTT frontiers (ur 1241
                    May 21<anchor n="1" xml:id="d58-f1"/>), Dept considers US, UK and France shd
                    proceed with delimitation all frontiers of FTT in territory presently under AMG
                    (Deptel 632 May 2<anchor n="2" xml:id="d58-f2"/>). You may advise FonOff
                    informally of Dept’s views, and express hope Itals will participate regardless
                    of Yugo decision.</p>
                <p>(Sent Rome as 787 rptd London as 2307 Moscow as 1239 Paris as 1950 and Belgrade
                    as 348.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="1" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d58-f2" n="2" xml:id="d58-f2-content">
                <p>Department telegram 281, May 2, to Belgrade, repeated to Rome as 632, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
